From 7c41b014d343796bd85a713d1d256410e7579929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:50:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Config: add the missing separator after
 FEX_APP_CACHE_LOCATION

GetCacheDirectory returned FEX_APP_CACHE_LOCATION verbatim, and its callers
append a subdirectory name (`cache/`, `codemap/`, ...). A location given
without a trailing slash, e.g. FEX_APP_CACHE_LOCATION=/tmp/x, put the code
cache in the sibling directory /tmp/xcache/ instead of /tmp/x/cache/.

Append the separator when it is missing.

Evidence: FEX_ENABLECODECACHINGWIP=1 FEX_CODECACHESCOPE=all
FEX_APP_CACHE_LOCATION=/tmp/fxpp-cache/x running a static x86-64 program
creates /tmp/fxpp-cache/xcodemap/ before this change and
/tmp/fxpp-cache/x/codemap/ after it (the code cache directory moves the
same way).

Ported from POWERarm d298034e5 (separator part only).
---
 Source/Common/Config.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/Common/Config.cpp b/Source/Common/Config.cpp
index 62bea17cd..9c07bf00e 100644
--- a/Source/Common/Config.cpp
+++ b/Source/Common/Config.cpp
@@ -704,7 +704,13 @@ fextl::string GetConfigDirectory(bool Global, const PortableInformation& Portabl
 fextl::string GetCacheDirectory() {
   const char* CacheOverride = getenv("FEX_APP_CACHE_LOCATION");
   if (CacheOverride) {
-    return CacheOverride;
+    // Callers append names (`cache/`, `codemap/`): without the separator a
+    // location of /tmp/x would put the code cache in /tmp/xcache/.
+    fextl::string Dir {CacheOverride};
+    if (!Dir.empty() && Dir.back() != '/') {
+      Dir += '/';
+    }
+    return Dir;
   }
 
 #ifndef _WIN32
